{"slug":"edit-distance","title":"The Fewest Edits to Turn One Word Into Another","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":742,"tags":["dp","edit-distance","string","two-strings"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Insert, delete or replace: the table over the prefixes has three neighbours","body":["You may change a word with three kinds of edit, each costing 1: **insert** a letter, **delete** a letter, or **replace** a letter by another. What is the smallest number of edits that turns the word `a` into the word `b`? For `horse` and `ros` the answer is 3: `horse -> rorse` (replace h by r) `-> rose` (delete r) `-> ros` (delete e). This number is known as the *Levenshtein distance*.","Let `dist(i, j)` be the smallest number of edits that turn the first `i` letters of `a` into the first `j` letters of `b`. Turning `i` letters into nothing needs `i` deletions, and turning nothing into `j` letters needs `j` insertions: `dist(i, 0) = i`, `dist(0, j) = j`. Otherwise look at the last letters. If `a[i] = b[j]`, nothing is needed for them: `dist(i, j) = dist(i - 1, j - 1)`. If they differ, take the cheapest of three edits: replace (`dist(i - 1, j - 1)`), delete `a[i]` (`dist(i - 1, j)`), insert `b[j]` (`dist(i, j - 1)`), and add 1: **`dist(i, j) = 1 + min of the three`**.",{"code":"prev = list(range(len(b) + 1))                   # dist(0, j) = j\nfor i in range(1, len(a) + 1):\n    cur = [i] + [0] * len(b)                     # dist(i, 0) = i\n    for j in range(1, len(b) + 1):\n        if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1]:\n            cur[j] = prev[j - 1]\n        else:\n            cur[j] = 1 + min(prev[j - 1], prev[j], cur[j - 1])\n    prev = cur\nprint(prev[len(b)])"},"The three neighbours of a cell are the cell above (a delete), the cell on the left (an insert) and the cell diagonally up-left (a replace or a match). With two rows the memory is O(|b|); the time is O(|a| * |b|) = one million steps at the limit. Spell checkers, DNA comparison and diff tools use this table."]},"statement":["Two words `a` and `b` are given. In one edit you may insert a letter anywhere, delete a letter, or replace a letter by another letter. Print the smallest number of edits that turns `a` into `b`."],"inputFormat":["The first line has the string `a`.","The second line has the string `b`."],"outputFormat":["Print the smallest number of edits."],"constraints":["1 <= length of a, length of b <= 1000","Both strings consist of lowercase English letters."],"examples":[{"input":"horse\nros\n","output":"3\n","note":"Replace h by r, delete r, delete e: 3 edits."},{"input":"abc\nabc\n","output":"0\n","note":"The words are equal: 0."}],"hints":["Let dist(i, j) be the answer for the first i letters of a and the first j letters of b; dist(i, 0) = i and dist(0, j) = j.","Equal last letters cost nothing: dist(i - 1, j - 1).","Different last letters: 1 + the smallest of the replace, delete and insert neighbours."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\na = input().strip()\nb = input().strip()\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string a;\n    cin >> a;\n    string b;\n    cin >> b;\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String a = next();\n        String b = next();\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["dist(i, j) is the smallest number of edits turning the first i letters of a into the first j letters of b: dist(i, 0) = i, dist(0, j) = j, dist(i - 1, j - 1) for equal last letters and otherwise 1 + the smallest of dist(i - 1, j - 1) (replace), dist(i - 1, j) (delete) and dist(i, j - 1) (insert). Two rows are kept."],"complexity":"Time O(|a| * |b|), space O(|b|).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\na = input().strip()\nb = input().strip()\n\nn = len(a)\nm = len(b)\nprev = list(range(m + 1))\nfor i in range(1, n + 1):\n    cur = [i] + [0] * m\n    ai = a[i - 1]\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        if ai == b[j - 1]:\n            cur[j] = prev[j - 1]\n        else:\n            best = prev[j - 1]\n            if prev[j] < best:\n                best = prev[j]\n            if cur[j - 1] < best:\n                best = cur[j - 1]\n            cur[j] = best + 1\n    prev = cur\nprint(prev[m])\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    string a;\n    cin >> a;\n    string b;\n    cin >> b;\n\n    int n = (int)a.size(), m = (int)b.size();\n    vector<int> prev(m + 1), cur(m + 1);\n    for (int j = 0; j <= m; j++) prev[j] = j;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        cur[0] = i;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {\n            if (a[i - 1] == b[j - 1]) cur[j] = prev[j - 1];\n            else cur[j] = 1 + min(prev[j - 1], min(prev[j], cur[j - 1]));\n        }\n        swap(prev, cur);\n    }\n    cout << prev[m] << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        String a = next();\n        String b = next();\n\n        int n = a.length(), m = b.length();\n        int[] prev = new int[m + 1];\n        int[] cur = new int[m + 1];\n        for (int j = 0; j <= m; j++) prev[j] = j;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n            cur[0] = i;\n            for (int j = 1; j <= m; j++) {\n                if (a.charAt(i - 1) == b.charAt(j - 1)) cur[j] = prev[j - 1];\n                else cur[j] = 1 + Math.min(prev[j - 1], Math.min(prev[j], cur[j - 1]));\n            }\n            int[] swap = prev;\n            prev = cur;\n            cur = swap;\n        }\n        System.out.println(prev[m]);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"horse\nros\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"abc\nabc\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"a\nb\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"a\naaaa\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"intention\nexecution\n","output":"5\n"},{"input":"bbbabbbabbabbbabbbbb\nababbbaabaabbbbbbaabbbbba\n","output":"8\n"},{"input":"cacccbbccaaaaabbacbaccbbbaccaababccaaabacacaacaaacccbaacaccabbaaaaabcaacacaaabcbaabacbababaaabccbaca\nccbbaccabbaccabacbccbbabccbbaaabbbaaaabbacccabbccbabcabcbabcbbaacacabcbbabccbaacccacbcabaccbbbbbccac\n","output":"49\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"205\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"210\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"881\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"298\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"441\n"},{"input":"b\\n","output":"999\n"},{"input":"\nb\n","output":"999\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"200\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"48\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"1000\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"\\n","output":"2\n"}]}